from __future__ import annotations
"""
Agentic Orchestrator (MCP over HTTP JSON)
----------------------------------------
- Always bootstrap TDNA once per session (internal-only): ask "What is the home airport?".
- Primary mode: users can just type free text (e.g., "please plan my trip…").
  We detect origin/destination/date-range from the text and trigger AIR + HOTEL + TDNA(history).
- If filters (origin/destination/dates) are provided in extra.filters, we use them too.
- Compose AIR + HOTEL answers and refine with TDNA travel history into one final reply.
- Falls back to the generic planner/critic loop if no trip details can be extracted.

Endpoints:
- POST /route_query
- POST /agent_query

Environment:
- HOTEL_MCP_URL, AIR_MCP_URL, TDNA_MCP_URL  (HTTP JSON-RPC endpoints for MCP servers)
- PASS_EXTRA_MODE in {"nested","flat","both"}  (how we pass extras to tool calls)
- BEDROCK_REGION, BEDROCK_MODEL_ID           (Claude 3.5 Sonnet defaults)
"""

